ObfuGuard
============

It's a fork of the original WireGuard, which adds a fearture
to pass a module parameter, which will be used to generate
random protocol messages' signatures

It's convinient to use the script `rebuildObfuguard.sh` from the source tree,
which gets only protocol's source, builds it and inserts it into the system.

HOW TO BUILD
==============

`make -C /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build M=./obfuguard_src/drivers/net/wireguard modules`

Then we need to remove the original WireGuard from the kernel, if you have it:
`rmmod wireguard | echo "The module wasn't loadeded..."`

Then we can insert it into the kernel with your own phrase to generate custom signatures
`insmod $(pwd)/$REPO_DIR_NAME/$DRIVER_DIR/wireguard.ko phrase="$YOUR_OBFU_PHRASE"`

dmesg will show you your obfuscate phrase and messages' signatures, which has been generated,
based on your phrase:

[46911.355581] wireguard: The module is loaded, using the obfuscate phrase: 1234567890
[46911.355582] wireguard: custom_signatures:
[46911.355583] wireguard: cookie_key_label[8]: 486C3277
[46911.355584] wireguard: handshake_name[37]: 0CF01E6B2985853D8FC74EB35FFDEB573BB4A
[46911.355585] wireguard: identifier_name[34]: A49928EFA2950F6BB8E4AD2D1F8D4BCD9F
[46911.355586] wireguard: mac1_key_label[8]: 41C887CC
[46911.355586] wireguard: wg_crypt[8]: 49B68C75
[46911.355587] wireguard: wg_kex[6]: 4FF296